./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000021-20260518-213407.log:1888:ralph/progress.txt:19252:  - The cross-tenant matrix is the SHARP distinction between a CapRead action and a CapDeploy action at this layer: for preview.read, Support is allowed cross-tenant via ReasonAllowedBySupport (the engine's `roleCaps.has(CapSupport) && (required == CapRead || required == CapSupport)` clause), while for preview.create / preview.delete Support is denied cross-tenant via ReasonDeniedCrossTenant. Pinning the Support cross-tenant ALLOW here is what keeps a future catalog change that downgraded preview.read out of the support exception detectable before it could regress incident-response read access.
